## Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
    input x content integer
    output o content integer

scope A:
    definition o equals -1
    exception definition o under condition x = 0 consequence equals 0
    exception definition o under condition x = 1 consequence equals 1
    exception definition o under condition x = 2 consequence equals 2
    exception definition o under condition x >= 3 and x < 20 consequence equals
        if Date.get_month of |2024-10-16| = x then 10 else 20
    exception definition o under condition x >= 20 consequence equals
        if Date.last_day_of_month of |2024-02-10| = |2024-02-29| and x=30 then 100 else 200
```

When encountering the condition that depends on a date operation we
don't yet encode symbolically, the engine explains this branch cannot
be investigated further, returns the concrete value it was still able
to compute, and then backtracks the same way if would if it had found
an error (by discarding the last constraint).

